<p>Read this page to get up to speed on what may be required. It can depend on which components you decide to use.</p>
<h2 id="php-and-composer">PHP and Composer<a class="anchor" href="#php-and-composer" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>PHP <strong>8.4.0 or newer</strong>, and Composer. Every v7 component declares <code>strict_types=1</code> in every source file
and requires <code>&gt;= 8.4.0</code>, so there's no partial upgrade path and no component that still runs on 8.3. CI
runs the suite on PHP 8.4 and 8.5.</p>
<h2 id="extensions-composer-enforces">Extensions Composer Enforces<a class="anchor" href="#extensions-composer-enforces" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>Six extensions are hard <code>require</code> entries rather than suggestions, so Composer resolves against them at
install time instead of letting you discover them at runtime:</p>
