<h2 id="extensions-each-component-would-like">Extensions Each Component Would Like<a class="anchor" href="#extensions-each-component-would-like" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>These are <code>suggest</code> entries. Composer never enforces them, an installation completes without them, and nothing
warns you at any point — so this table is the one to read against what you actually plan to use:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>For</th>
<th>Extensions</th>
<th>Wanted by</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Databases</td>
<td><code>ext-pdo</code>, <code>ext-mysqli</code>, <code>ext-pgsql</code>, <code>ext-sqlite3</code></td>
<td><code>pop-db</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Images</td>
<td><code>ext-imagick</code>, <code>ext-ctype</code></td>
<td><code>pop-image</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>PDFs</td>
<td><code>ext-imagick</code>, <code>ext-iconv</code>, <code>ext-mbstring</code>, <code>ext-zlib</code></td>
<td><code>pop-pdf</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Queues</td>
<td><code>ext-redis</code></td>
<td><code>pop-queue</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Caching</td>
<td><code>ext-apcu</code>, <code>ext-redis</code>, <code>ext-memcached</code></td>
<td><code>pop-cache</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>HTTP</td>
<td><code>ext-zlib</code>, <code>ext-mbstring</code>, <code>ext-simplexml</code></td>
<td><code>pop-http</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Config and locale files</td>
<td><code>ext-simplexml</code>, <code>ext-libxml</code></td>
<td><code>pop-config</code>, <code>pop-i18n</code>, <code>pop-form</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
